📣 CEO VanEck: Most crypto projects will disappear!

Jan van Eck believes that in the next 5-10 years, the crypto market will become much more selective, with only a few major players surviving.

In his opinion, most tokens lack sustainable competitive advantages.

➠ $BTC will remain one of the leading digital assets;
➠ $BTC  will continue to compete with gold for reserve asset status;
➠ Bitcoin's market capitalization could reach approximately half that of gold;
➠ VanEck considers 2026 a weak point in the post-halving cycle;
➠ The GENIUS Act could become one of the most important laws for the financial system.

VanEck also believes that 2026 is becoming the "year of enterprise blockchains," as JPMorgan, BNY Mellon, and other companies are actively building their own infrastructure.
